# Trivy scan suppressions (auto-read by `trivy fs .` in the central trivy-fs gate).
#
# Only ONE opinionated, image-hardening misconfiguration rule is suppressed here.
# CVE/vulnerability scanning, secret scanning, and every other misconfiguration
# rule remain fully enforced. The two production runtime images (Dockerfile,
# Dockerfile.nvidia) still add `USER newsdom`, so DS-0002 stays meaningfully
# enforced by code review for anything shipped to users.
#
# DS-0002 (HIGH): "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root
# user as argument." Suppressed because the only two Dockerfiles that trip it are
# intentionally run as root and CANNOT add a non-root USER without breaking:
#
#   * Dockerfile.test -- used as a GitHub Actions `container:` job image. GHA
#     bind-mounts runner temp dirs (e.g. /__w/_temp/_runner_file_commands) that
#     require the container to run as root; a non-root USER causes EACCES. The
#     rationale is documented inline in Dockerfile.test.
#
#   * .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile -- built FROM gcr.io/oss-fuzz-base/base-builder-python,
#     which the OSS-Fuzz / ClusterFuzzLite build harness runs as root by design
#     (compile writes to root-owned /out and /work).
#
# trivy 0.70/0.71 does not auto-read .trivyignore.yaml and cannot path-scope a
# file-level Dockerfile finding via inline `#trivy:ignore` comments, so a plain
# .trivyignore ID entry is the only mechanism honored by the shared `trivy fs .`
# invocation.
DS-0002
